  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Dry forecast holds for next 6-7 days\n\nWidespread freezing conditions will be tough to come by across\nLebanon and Lancaster Counties, but typically colder valleys\nwill see temps dip to 31-32F and fairly widespread frost should\noccur elsewhere throughout the Freeze Warning.\n\nA sprawling ridge of high pressure stretching from Southeastern Canada\nthrough the Mid Atlantic Region and into the Southeastern U.S. \nwill remain nearly stationary over the next 7 days. This will \nkeep the probability for measurable rain at zero here in \nPennsylvania during this period.\n\nSunny skies will prevail across the CWA today with high \ntemperatures mainly in the upper 50s to low 60s, though the \nhighest ridges will only reach the mid 50s. Lows tonight will \nbe similar to those this morning (upper 20s to mid 30s) and \nhighs Sunday afternoon will be about 2 degrees warmer than \ntoday.\n\nA pair of weak, moisture-starved cold fronts and flat northern \nstream short waves, will drift SE from the from the Upper Great\nLakes Mon night-Tues and late Thurs into early Friday, but PoPs\nare hardly worth having as PWATs stay very low with each.\n\nLater next week into at least Saturday (10/31), the wetter \ntrending GFS members have flipped toward the drier EC with a \nnotable upper level ridge building over the Ohio Valley and Mid \nAtlantic Region.",
